{# ===========================================================================
   Component: location-jump

   Four anchors, not a table of contents: Hours, Menu, FAQ, Order, the things
   a Maps visitor actually arrives wanting, per the mobile audit. Sits right
   after the NAP plate, before components/location-place.njk.

   NOT STICKY. The compact header (src/js/header-scroll.js) already handles
   staying reachable while scrolled; a second sticky element would fight it
   for the same 61px of headroom.

   EACH LINK IS GATED ON THE SECTION IT POINTS TO ACTUALLY RENDERING. A room
   with no confirmed FAQ or no order URL does not get a link to a section
   that is not there; same rule components/location-faq.njk and
   components/location-order.njk already apply to themselves. Hours has no
   gate: even a room with no confirmed hours (Maui) still renders the
   "Call the room" fallback inside the same #hours plate row, which is still
   somewhere worth jumping to.

   USAGE
     {% set loc = ... %}
     {% include "components/location-jump.njk" %}
   =========================================================================== #}
{%- set jumpRoom = roomMenus.byRoom[loc.id] %}
{%- set jumpHasMenu = jumpRoom and jumpRoom.sections | length %}
{%- set jumpHasFaq = (locationFaq[loc.id] | default([])) | length %}
{%- set jumpHasOrder = loc.orderUrl %}

<nav class="jump" aria-label="Jump to a section on this page">
  <div class="jump__inner">
    <a class="jump__link" href="#hours">Hours</a>
    {%- if jumpHasMenu %}
    <a class="jump__link" href="#menu">Menu</a>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if jumpHasFaq %}
    <a class="jump__link" href="#faq-title">FAQ</a>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if jumpHasOrder %}
    <a class="jump__link" href="#order-title">Order</a>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</nav>
